  "worked_solution": "Notice that our inequality\n\n$$\nx(x+2)<0\n$$\n\n \n\nis a \"*less than*\" inequality. Therefore, we need to find the values of $x$ for which the parabola \n\n$$\ny=x(x+2)\n$$\n\nis *below *the $x$-axis. We mark these values of $x$ in blue in the diagram below.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13972108/assets/45ecefb7d229f6882bc4e5cd4b3583e65a295c83cdd4de83d9d8fa3719e33b54.png)\n\nSo, the solution to the inequality is $-2<x<0.$",
